WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.840
Escha.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:04.220
Escha.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.810
Escha.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.780
Oh.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.040
You are here again.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.500
Hey, Clone, what is the name of that place?

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:30.300
I don't know. Nobody has ever been there, and that's why they call it the Unexplored Ruin.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.120
I wonder if anyone lives up there? Perhaps a prince or a princess?

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.050
I wonder too.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.310
I want to go there one day.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.240
Hey, what's for supper tonight?

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.960
Good morning!

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.000
Good morning, Escha. Faul would like to talk to you.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.800
Dad, did you need something?

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.130
Hm?

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:47.150
Oh, I was just thinking that ever since you started working at the branch, you've gotten a lot better at alchemy.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.780
I've been learning a lot by finishing my requests.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.620
My oh my, that's wonderful.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.400
Since you have gotten so much better, I have just the thing for you.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.120
I want you to come up with a way to improve the apple orchard's yield.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:11.360
Faul thought that since you are a fully-fledged alchemist, you might be able to think of a few new ideas.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.330
Me? Fully-fledged?

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.210
Please.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.800
Improving the orchard's yield, huh?

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.410
That's right. It's a request from my father and Clone.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:28.310
It's not really an official assignment, but a personal request for me.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.230
We should be able to ask everyone for help since we aren't very busy right now.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.480
Still, that's a hard one.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.070
It's true that the soil here depletes if you don't take care of it.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.910
Can't we use fertilisers or pesticides?

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.280
We can try some new products that are known to be effective.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.660
We can ask my family's company to help, too.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:53.150
Thanks, but even though it might help right now,

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.170
those kinds of things might hurt the harvest in the long run.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.030
I guess you're right.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.300
This is quite a difficult problem.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.300
Just thinking about it won't get us anywhere.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.730
It's nice outside, so let's head over to the orchard.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.490
Escha-senpai's family's apple orchard is really big.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.310
Yeah.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:20.020
Huh? Nio-san, are you here to help?

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:22.610
Yep, even if it's just a little, I wanted to help.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.520
He's throwing away the unripe apples.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.620
What he's doing is called fruit thinning.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.370
Fruit thinning?

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.750
They're leaving the larger fruits,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.960
and throwing out the others before they start to ripen in autumn.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.690
Is that to make sure only big apples grow?

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.330
That's one reason.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:50.110
If you let all the fruits grow, it'll wear the tree out,

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:53.640
and that might hurt the harvest yield next year.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.400
So this is actually an important task.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.700
Thanks for your help. Let's take a break.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.920
I suddenly found myself helping out.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:06.780
Same here.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.530
Thanks, everyone!

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.080
It feels like a waste if we just discard these.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.710
Even though they're so small, they're still apples.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.770
You can take some home if you want.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:18.790
Really?

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.250
Even if we keep them, we only use them as fertiliser.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:25.270
How about if we try to use them to cook?

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:26.760
Yep, I agree!

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.220
Please let me help too!

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:34.990
<i>I hope Escha hasn't forgotten about the request to improve the orchard's yield.</i>

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:40.710
So bitter and sour.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.440
This doesn't taste good

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.280
I guess not.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.140
Now I can see why these usually get thrown out.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.450
But these still smell like apples and taste somewhat sweet.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.990
Maybe we can make desserts out of these.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:55.040
I love apple desserts!

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.130
If we try to make pies or tarts out of these, they might not taste very good because of how small these are.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.880
I guess we need to think of new recipes.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:06.510
What's that? Did I hear somebody talking about desserts just now?

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.800
She has really sharp hearing.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.210
Aren't you good at making desserts too, Wilbell-san?

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.760
Desserts? Of course!

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.730
There's nothing I can't do!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:20.500
Oh, do you want to make desserts using unwanted apples?

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.190
I can smell business already.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.580
No, we aren't saying that we want to turn this into a product.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.150
That's sweet, Logy-san.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.640
As sweet as ripe apples.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:35.760
Understand? Colseit's speciality apples can only be harvested in autumn.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:41.290
If we could make something out of these unripe apples, we would have a summer speciality too.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.540
This is a huge opportunity!

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.640
Is that so?

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.510
I'll start making my own desserts too!

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:53.970
Everyone, effective immediately, those recipes you are holding cost 10,000 cole each.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.930
Oh? That's quite an interesting idea.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:01.690
Huh? Did you have desserts on your menu, Duke?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:06.010
Nope. I get mostly male customers, after all.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:11.250
If I added desserts to the menu, maybe I'll get more girls to come.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.280
There's that too.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.200
The Fourth Annual King of Eating Championship?

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.630
Duke-san, you're holding another one?

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:22.170
Again?

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:26.920
The Dragon's Fist holds an eating competition from time to time.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:31.630
You just told us that you wanted more girls to visit, and here you are, planning something so crass.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.390
There's no way a girl would come for something like this.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.590
I thought that would be the case.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:41.890
And that's why I was thinking. What if I held a dessert contest at the same time?

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.850
A dessert contest?

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:49.810
That's right. Aren't you girls trying to make desserts out of unripe apples right now?

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:52.820
Let's hold a contest to find the most delicious dessert.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.330
We'll hold it at the same time as the King of Eating Championship,

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.750
and the winners of each contest will get ten free meal tickets for the restaurant.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.290
That sounds like it'll be lots of fun!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.180
Ten free meal tickets? That's a lot!

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.790
That's getting me worked up!

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.770
Winning the contest...

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:14.550
...and earning big bucks from selling Katla Brand desserts made with unripe apples. Isn't this a great opportunity?

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.820
I recall seeing a dessert cookbook at home.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.760
Everyone's so enthusiastic.

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:23.850
Just a moment, Logy.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:27.560
You'll be entering the King of Eating Championship, right?

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:28.740
M-Me?

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.780
Don't be shy. All the young lads your age eat like a horse.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.670
How about if you go find me some more participants?

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:38.990
Thanks so much!

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.310
Come back hungry!

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:52.920
Huh? Logy, you're joining the King of Eating Championship too?

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:55.110
More like Duke-san is making me.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.410
On top of that, he's forcing me to find people to join.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.350
Sounds just like Duke-san.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.350
Got it. I'll join.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:05.520
Marion, it's time for a break.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.070
How thoughtful of you.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.730
Let's see. There's tea and... this cake looks delicious!

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.210
Where'd you get it?

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.270
I made it.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.790
I heard that they are holding a dessert-making contest.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.400
I thought it'd be nice to join and tried my hand at making one.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:23.540
How is it, Marion?

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:27.370
Linca, have you tasted it yourself?

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.290
Taste? What is that?

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.300
Just a little more sugar.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:39.300
Just wait and see. The homunculi definitely like my desserts more.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.220
What are you doing, Solle?

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.270
N-Nothing at all, Branch Manager!

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.190
I'm just thinking about a dessert recipe.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:48.840
The contest at Duke's place, huh?

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:52.100
You've always been fond of desserts.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:54.570
You're even having <i>this</i> for lunch.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.650
Y-You too, Branch Manager?

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:59.570
I thought I would eat the same thing as you sometimes.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.540
I-I see, Branch Manager.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:06.500
Solle, there is no need to call me Branch Manager when we are alone.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.630
Yes, Father.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:12.440
They're family?

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:16.420
I probably shouldn't interfere. I won't ask them then.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:23.310
Huh? Escha, you aren't thinking of your recipe for the dessert contest?

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:27.350
Well, actually, I couldn't find a way to improve the orchard's yield.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:31.600
If it were that easy, someone would have thought of it already.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.110
Huh?

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:34.850
What's the matter?

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.030
Now that I think about it,

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:42.770
wouldn't your father and Clone both know that it's not easy to improve the harvest yield?

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:43.490
Yes.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:47.250
If that's the case, what are they expecting from you?

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.210
You're right.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:54.420
Huh?

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:59.840
The colour of the slope there is kind of different.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.340
It gets plenty sunshine too.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:06.720
Huh?!

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.640
What was that just now?

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:13.480
This is bad!

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.400
Are you okay?!

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.860
What's this?

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.210
Geez, Wilbell-san!

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:25.080
I'm sorry!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.740
What's going on? I heard a big explosion.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.830
Huh? You must be mistaken.

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:34.830
That's why I told you to be careful when you use your magic!

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.340
What? Magic?

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:42.680
W-Well, didn't you say before that you wanted to taste the desserts I make with magic?

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.100
I did try to control the magic, but still...

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:48.510
So what happened to the dessert?

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:49.520
About that...

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:53.520
Mine was almost done.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.930
Let's try once more! Okay?

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:00.250
That's right! The contest is tomorrow!

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.800
Let's cheer up and do this again!

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.140
Watch what you're doing with your magic this time.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:07.840
Okay.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.880
Okay! All the challengers are here now.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.670
I'll explain the rules.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:23.300
Dessert Contest participants, go make your desserts in the kitchen.

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:27.370
You can use any ingredient or tool. Feel free to use anything you brought with you.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:28.180
Yes!

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:32.730
After that has started, the long-awaited King of Eating Championship begins.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.150
I'll keep bringing them dishes out.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.610
The last one standing wins!

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.070
Yeah!

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:43.280
Huh? Weren't you going to join the Dessert Contest, Linca-san?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.880
Marion has forbidden me from joining.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.410
I had no choice but to join this one instead.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.370
Why did she forbid you?

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.900
I don't know.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:54.750
Marion sometimes says things that nobody understands.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.140
Hm...

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:59.890
Escha, have you thought up a dessert recipe?

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:02.370
Yes, somehow.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:04.110
Did you not have enough time?

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.180
Actually, I...

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.600
Let's see...

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.520
We have this cookbook and this...

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.060
Hm?

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:15.310
Oh, it's <i>the Adventures of the Hummingbird Princess</i>!

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:18.610
It's the sequel to the last one!

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:23.610
Before I knew it, I was totally engrossed in the book.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.510
Something similar to this happened before.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.350
Yes, it did.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.320
Well, do your best.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.780
Yes!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.750
Okay! Let's start making the desserts!

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.810
All right! Now let the King of Eating Championship begin!

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:00.520
This is quite a lot.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.690
This is amazing!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:03.980
I'll dig in.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:08.110
This is just the appetiser. You can do it.

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.480
I can't do it.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.680
I'm giving up too.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.070
Logy and Awin are out.

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:35.180
It's down to Reyfer and Linca!

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.060
Seconds!

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.230
That's a lot.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:46.130
This might be overdoing it...

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:49.200
Don't push yourself too hard, Swordsgirl.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.950
Oh, don't worry.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.670
I skipped breakfast today. Finishing this is no problem.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:58.050
What do you usually eat for breakfast?

00:14:58.050 --> 00:14:59.160
I'll dig in now.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.260
I-I'm at my limit.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:11.510
Thanks for the meal.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:16.810
Our champion, who didn't slow down one bit, is Linca-san!

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:19.810
I made the right choice skipping breakfast.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.220
Just what are you?

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:24.690
It's done!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.110
We're finished!

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.490
Then let the Dessert Contest begin!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:36.830
Speaking of which, who gets to judge this contest?

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:40.890
The person who picks the winner is the King of Eating, Linca-san!

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:42.410
Me?

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:49.170
If a dessert can get somebody who's full to say it's good, then it must be quite the delicacy.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:50.570
I see!

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:51.930
That makes sense.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:55.430
Understood. I'll dig in, then.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:05.430
As I watch her eat, I get the feeling that she isn't <i>that</i> full.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:06.270
Yeah.

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:10.240
Thanks for the food!

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.450
So? Which one's the best?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.990
All of them are so good,

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.950
but if I have to pick one...

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:19.410
It's this one!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.720
Oh, that's...!

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:25.580
Those are the cookies that I made!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:28.880
Yay! Awesome!

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.630
I won!

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.260
You did it, Wilbell-san!

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.850
Thanks, but that's just how good I am.

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:36.890
Yay!

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.890
So? Why did you pick that one?

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:41.350
Somehow, each cookie tasted a little different,

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.310
but they all tasted great!

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:47.400
Yay! Yay!

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:47.400
Oh, that's brilliant.

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:53.820
<i>Although Wilbell-san won, it's wonderful how everyone's desserts are full of personality.</i>

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.820
<i>Maybe that's all I need to do.</i>

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.160
What's up, Escha?

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:05.050
Logy-san, would you mind helping me tomorrow?

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:36.700
Yay! It's done!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.790
Dad, Clone,

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:44.620
here's what we made.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.600
It's fertiliser.

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:47.370
Soil?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:52.270
Yup, we used alchemy to condense different nutrients.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:56.060
We took soil from around the only flower blooming in a barren land,

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:58.790
and soil from an oasis within a desert.

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:01.140
We made it with all sorts of soil!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:03.560
With this, the soil will act as a natural fertiliser,

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.590
and the orchard's yield will improve!

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:09.010
My oh my, that's an interesting way to see it.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.610
Escha thought of it.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.820
I realised during the Dessert Contest.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.210
Although Wilbell-san won the contest,

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:17.530
everyone's desserts were wonderful.

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:22.780
What's important is not what's right, but what we believe is right.

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:29.690
So that's who Escha Malier is, right?

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.630
Follow me.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.210
I wonder what this is about.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:38.050
I'll leave it to you, Clone.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:41.320
If I remember correctly, this slope is...

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:43.810
Escha, this place is yours.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:46.270
Huh? What do you mean?

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:50.880
Did you notice that the apple trees on this slope have different colours?

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:51.930
Yep.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:56.780
This plot of land is divided into blocks and handed to the Malier family's alchemists to care for.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:01.470
Escha, your predecessors have been alchemists for generations,

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:06.540
and all of them have come up with different ways to try to improve this apple orchard.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:11.210
That's why the slope's colour is different.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:15.500
There have been attempts both good and bad. Sometimes the apples even rotted.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.820
Through these many attempts, the apple orchard expanded bit by bit,

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:22.110
and its harvest improved as a result.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.110
So this is...

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:26.650
This is the plot managed by Miria.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:28.310
This was Mum's?!

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:33.190
She passed away at a young age, and didn't have the chance to try much.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:38.690
Escha, I want you to experiment here and take on Miria's share too.

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:42.150
One day, this plot will reflect your personality,

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:45.760
and will lead the apple orchard to prosperity.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:57.340
I will do my best!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.480
Just watch, Clone!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.090
Watch, Mum!

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:13.310
I propose a toast in honour of my victory, to Wilbell voll-Erslied!

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:14.860
Cheers!

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.320
Cheers!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:19.750
Thanks for coming all the way here to celebrate with me!

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:22.490
We got some of the desserts left over from the contest.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.570
Let's eat them together!

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.530
I've wanted to try them!

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:29.050
This is great!

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:34.370
That reminds me. Wasn't Duke-san going to add the winning dessert to his menu?

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:38.210
Oh, that. I declined.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:41.290
Huh? That's such a waste!

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:45.180
I actually added my magic to each and every cookie.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:48.680
Although each one is delicious in its own way,

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:51.640
I can't make enough for him to add to the menu.

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.100
Katla-san said she wanted to mass produce them to sell.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:57.570
There's no way that will happen.

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:00.050
I see. What a shame.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:03.060
Well, if you just want to eat it here, I can make some for you girls again.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:05.060
Great.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:09.510
Hey, Escha-chan, didn't you mention something about a picture book before the contest?

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:13.910
Yes, when I was looking for a recipe, I found a really nostalgic picture book.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:17.250
These are picture books that Clone wrote!

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.830
So they're the only copies?

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:22.510
You should read them to us.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.390
Yes!

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.990
"Adventures of the Hummingbird Princess."

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:35.230
"The Hummingbird Princess is clever and popular."

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:39.370
"However, she is also somewhat selfish."

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:15.650
"Tell me, Hummingbird Princess,"

00:23:15.650 --> 00:23:20.330
"Why won't the vegetables in Grandfather's fields grow?"

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:23.540
Don't talk to me.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.620
I don't like humans.

00:23:26.620 --> 00:23:28.170
I hate them.
